776:\item \textbf{Classifier family = generative family.} 98.9\% is a lower bound, not the Bayes rate.
792:\textbf{Multiplicity:} All p-values survive Bonferroni (630 total family; \S7.3); \S8.21 rows keep the historical 610-way annotation. \textbf{Normality:} profit distributions are unimodal and approximately symmetric at seed level; paired t-test robust at n = 50. \textbf{Equivalence testing:} ``Within \$4 of the oracle'' is descriptive --- the \$3.87 gap is significant (p = 1.3e-13). ``Essentially matches'' claims should carry the caveat that differences are statistically detectable at n = 50 even when economically negligible.
